### Six failures, one refresh decision

<figure class="stepper"><span class="stepper-title">Trace two requests using an expired credential</span><div class="stage viz-stack"><div class="node" data-el="a"><strong>Request A</strong><small data-text="aV">—</small></div><div class="node" data-el="b"><strong>Request B</strong><small data-text="bV">—</small></div><div class="node" data-el="token"><strong>Token storage</strong><small data-text="tokenV">—</small></div><div class="node" data-el="refresh"><strong>Dedicated refresh API</strong><small data-text="refreshV">—</small></div></div><script type="application/json" class="steps">[
{
"label": "Expired token",
"caption": "Both calls leave with token T1. This is a schematic successful refresh path, not a promise that every 401 is recoverable.",
"state": {
"a": "active",
"b": "active"
},
"text": {
"aV": "sent T1",
"bV": "sent T1",
"tokenV": "T1",
"refreshV": "idle"
},
"add": [
"a",
"b",
"token",
"refresh"
]
},
{
"label": "A wins the refresh",
"caption": "The authenticator serializes access, checks stored credentials and makes one bounded refresh call.",
"state": {
"a": "warn",
"refresh": "active"
},
"text": {
"aV": "401 → refresh decision",
"refreshV": "request new credential"
}
},
{
"label": "A stores T2",
"caption": "After a successful refresh, A stores T2 and returns a follow-up request.",
"state": {
"token": "done",
"a": "active",
"refresh": "done"
},
"text": {
"tokenV": "T2",
"aV": "follow-up uses T2",
"refreshV": "finished"
}
},
{
"label": "B rechecks",
"caption": "B reaches the same decision later. Storage differs from its failed Authorization header, so it can reuse T2.",
"state": {
"b": "active"
},
"text": {
"bV": "follow-up uses T2"
}
},
{
"label": "Bound the outcome",
"caption": "If recovery fails or a further challenge exceeds the allowed count, return no follow-up. The repository must handle the failure.",
"state": {
"a": "done",
"b": "done"
},
"text": {
"aV": "success or terminal failure",
"bV": "success or terminal failure"
}
}
]</script><figcaption>Follow the original authenticator example below the ownership map. Use a separate refresh client and test concurrent challenges, cancellation and refresh failure.</figcaption></figure>

